{"name":"Amish Green","hex":"#3a5f4e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Amish","blocks":[{"text":"The Amish, formally the Old Order Amish, are a group of traditionalist Anabaptist Christian church fellowships with Swiss and Alsatian origins. Because they maintain a degree of separation from surrounding populations, and hold their faith in common, the Amish have been described by certain scholars as an ethnoreligious group, combining features of an ethnicity and a Christian denomination. The Amish are closely related to Old Order Mennonites and Conservative Mennonites, denominations that are also a part of Anabaptist Christianity. The Amish are known for simple living, plain dress, Christian pacifism, and slowness to adopt many conveniences of modern technology, with a view neither to interrupt family time, nor replace face-to-face conversations whenever possible, and a view to maintain self-sufficiency. The Amish value rural life, manual labor, humility and Gelassenheit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Lancaster_County_Amish_03.jpg/330px-Lancaster_County_Amish_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amish"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Amish_cover.jpg/250px-Amish_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/Amish_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Amish_cover.jpg/250px-Amish_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cover of The Amish and the Mennonites, 1938","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmish_cover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Amish_cemetery.gif/500px-Amish_cemetery.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Amish_cemetery.gif/500px-Amish_cemetery.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An old Amish cemetery in Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, 1941","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmish_cemetery.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Flickr_-_Nicholas_T_-_Bright.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_Nicholas_T_-_Bright.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Flickr_-_Nicholas_T_-_Bright.jpg/1280px-Flickr_-_Nicholas_T_-_Bright.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Flickr_-_Nicholas_T_-_Bright.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_Nicholas_T_-_Bright.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red barns are common on Amish farms.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlickr_-_Nicholas_T_-_Bright.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/US_30_farms.JPG/500px-US_30_farms.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/US_30_farms.JPG/1280px-US_30_farms.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/US_30_farms.JPG/500px-US_30_farms.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A view of Amish farms from westbound US 30","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUS_30_farms.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/De_Ausbund_329.jpg/500px-De_Ausbund_329.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/De_Ausbund_329.jpg/500px-De_Ausbund_329.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A scan of the historical document Diß Lied haben die sieben Brüder im Gefängnüß zu Gmünd gemacht","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADe_Ausbund_329.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Amish_youth_groups_at_Behalt_7.jpg/500px-Amish_youth_groups_at_Behalt_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Amish_youth_groups_at_Behalt_7.jpg/500px-Amish_youth_groups_at_Behalt_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Amish youth learning about a church before considering membership","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmish_youth_groups_at_Behalt_7.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Amish_Farmhouse.jpg/500px-Amish_Farmhouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Amish_Farmhouse.jpg/500px-Amish_Farmhouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clothing is plain in style and sewn by hand.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmish_Farmhouse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Amish_market.jpg/500px-Amish_market.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Amish_market.jpg/1280px-Amish_market.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Amish_market.jpg/500px-Amish_market.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Amish food sold at a market","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmish_market.jpg"}],"sounds":{"green":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-green.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f6/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-green.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-green.wav